00:47:28,000 --> 00:47:29,280
Carrots in the hotel.

812
00:47:30,240 --> 00:47:36,020
Yes, no, we're gonna make it a... two-minute prediction, because it's gonna be a while until we're there.

813
00:47:38,600 --> 00:47:40,080
These fucking predictions, man.

814
00:47:40,460 --> 00:47:42,000
It kind of cracks me up, you know?

815
00:47:43,580 --> 00:47:44,920
Rat Ray style, just...

816
00:47:44,880 --> 00:47:45,680
Gamble on everything.

817
00:47:49,440 --> 00:47:51,100
I want to see big bets on this.

818
00:47:55,780 --> 00:47:57,640
I'm raising a generation of gamblers.

819
00:47:58,620 --> 00:47:59,400
Fake gambling!

820
00:47:59,520 --> 00:48:00,560
It's not real gambling, guys.

821
00:48:00,720 --> 00:48:01,380
Just for the future.

822
00:48:02,040 --> 00:48:05,100
We're having fun, you know, gambling made-up potatoes.

823
00:48:05,540 --> 00:48:06,640
That don't mean anything.

824
00:48:07,200 --> 00:48:08,220
It doesn't mean anything.

825
00:48:08,960 --> 00:48:10,540
Except, of course, bragging powers.

826
00:48:12,220 --> 00:48:13,860
Okay, the Danish island is somewhere there.

827
00:48:17,620 --> 00:48:18,600
I gotta fix that.

828
00:48:18,720 --> 00:48:19,600
Maybe I'll do that off-stream.

829
00:48:19,740 --> 00:48:20,240
I'm not even kidding.

830
00:48:20,380 --> 00:48:21,000
I'm actually not kidding.

831
00:48:21,180 --> 00:48:22,380
I will go here and fix this.

832
00:48:23,400 --> 00:48:24,460
It's not the first time.

833
00:48:24,860 --> 00:48:26,440
Or, I mean, it wouldn't be the first time.

834
00:48:28,520 --> 00:48:29,220
There's the island.

835
00:48:30,500 --> 00:48:33,380
On the northeastern ridge of the island... Oh, wait, there's two.

836
00:48:36,780 --> 00:48:37,860
Or is it just one?

837
00:48:39,200 --> 00:48:39,560
Connected.

838
00:48:40,900 --> 00:48:41,960
It may be just one.

839
00:48:45,300 --> 00:48:47,780
Most people are saying no to the carrots in the hotel.

840
00:48:49,060 --> 00:48:49,460
Interesting.

841
00:48:53,120 --> 00:48:53,920
I'm gonna go there.

842
00:48:54,060 --> 00:48:56,780
I'm gonna make sure that the believers are winning this one.

843
00:48:56,900 --> 00:48:59,200
Because I almost want to believe in myself, of course.

844
00:48:59,340 --> 00:49:00,580
I want there to be carrots.

845
00:49:04,880 --> 00:49:09,500
Let's just say that the doubters have a record of, you know, being wrong on this channel.

846
00:49:10,780 --> 00:49:11,880
They are usually wrong.

847
00:49:12,360 --> 00:49:18,460
Actually, I think statistically, if you're a doubter, in anything I do, in any game, chances are you're going to lose.

848
00:49:21,400 --> 00:49:22,780
Just want to put that out there, you know?

849
00:49:26,420 --> 00:49:27,940
You can still change your mind.

850
00:49:28,140 --> 00:49:28,620
Seven seconds.

851
00:49:31,970 --> 00:49:32,970
Remember, it's rigged.

852
00:49:34,350 --> 00:49:35,330
Oh, too late!

853
00:49:36,270 --> 00:49:36,990
It's locked.

854
00:49:37,250 --> 00:49:38,330
Uh-oh, we got face timers?

855
00:49:39,830 --> 00:49:40,550
No thanks.

856
00:49:46,890 --> 00:49:48,430
Now, it wasn't that far away.

857
00:49:48,690 --> 00:49:50,370
It just felt kind of close, right?

858
00:49:50,490 --> 00:49:51,530
Because we were flying.

859
00:49:58,350 --> 00:49:58,710
Ha!

860
00:49:58,830 --> 00:49:59,190
I won.

861
00:49:59,330 --> 00:50:00,170
He looked that way first.

862
00:50:02,250 --> 00:50:02,950
Staring contest.

863
00:50:03,110 --> 00:50:06,050
I can never do that in real life because my eyes get so dry, you know.

864
00:50:06,670 --> 00:50:06,990
Woo!

865
00:50:10,030 --> 00:50:11,070
There's a village over there.

866
00:50:11,150 --> 00:50:12,130
We can check that on the way home.

867
00:50:14,230 --> 00:50:16,170
Could be a good option to gamble on as well.

868
00:50:17,490 --> 00:50:18,750
In case we don't find a carrot.

869
00:50:20,010 --> 00:50:23,330
So this is the northeastern ridge right here, so it's that way.

870
00:50:29,880 --> 00:50:32,820
It may actually be in that place over there.

871
00:50:34,940 --> 00:50:35,840
That forest.

872
00:50:43,000 --> 00:50:43,540
Oh.

873
00:50:49,740 --> 00:50:50,920
I already took that.

874
00:50:59,980 --> 00:51:03,400
Dude, I just burped like crazy, and you will never have known.

875
00:51:03,700 --> 00:51:05,040
Because I muted it in time.

876
00:51:06,580 --> 00:51:07,620
You will never know.

877
00:51:08,180 --> 00:51:10,880
In fact, I do all kinds of things while muted, all the time.

878
00:51:11,160 --> 00:51:12,400
And you will never know.

879
00:51:13,120 --> 00:51:13,940
Isn't that amazing?

880
00:51:16,780 --> 00:51:23,180
The power of technology allows me to be a degenerate without anyone knowing.

881
00:51:24,860 --> 00:51:26,660
It's pretty normal to burp, I guess.

882
00:51:33,450 --> 00:51:35,390
Okay, I'm actually getting a little lost.

883
00:51:38,030 --> 00:51:41,950
I think we're gonna have to, you know, elevate ourselves slightly.

884
00:51:44,190 --> 00:51:45,450
Just to get a look around.

885
00:51:45,650 --> 00:51:47,850
Because I'm not used to being on this ground level.

886
00:51:52,270 --> 00:51:53,330
Yeah, I don't know where I am.

887
00:51:54,690 --> 00:51:56,430
It was kind of a straight shot, though, you know?

888
00:51:57,550 --> 00:52:00,950
I flew in a straight line southwest from where the hotel was.

889
00:52:03,270 --> 00:52:04,110
Should be over here.

890
00:52:06,890 --> 00:52:09,690
The good news is, it's gonna be easy to find when we find it.

891
00:52:10,430 --> 00:52:11,650
It's kind of a big place.

892
00:52:15,060 --> 00:52:16,960
Or in a better way, it's hard to miss.

893
00:52:17,200 --> 00:52:17,720
Wait, did I see it?

894
00:52:19,920 --> 00:52:20,860
I think I just saw it.

895
00:52:24,300 --> 00:52:26,040
I saw the outline of it, I believe.

896
00:52:27,880 --> 00:52:28,740
Saw something dark.

897
00:52:32,200 --> 00:52:32,520
No.

898
00:52:33,820 --> 00:52:34,420
Wait, what?

899
00:52:36,760 --> 00:52:37,660
No, we're cooked!

900
00:52:37,840 --> 00:52:38,640
I don't know where it is!

901
00:52:42,930 --> 00:52:43,930
Emergency elevation.

902
00:52:49,110 --> 00:52:51,270
Did I really cross that amount of water?

903
00:52:53,690 --> 00:52:54,710
Aw, frick.

904
00:52:57,010 --> 00:52:58,750
I think we're gonna have to go in the water again.

905
00:53:01,930 --> 00:53:02,430
Wee!

906
00:53:02,590 --> 00:53:03,610
Almost forgot I could fly.

907
00:53:07,390 --> 00:53:07,890
Speed.

908
00:53:15,260 --> 00:53:17,400
My ears are itchy for some reason.

909
00:53:30,740 --> 00:53:32,860
I'm still going exactly northeast.

910
00:53:33,960 --> 00:53:38,040
This is still the normal along the cows... ridge line.

911
00:53:43,510 --> 00:53:47,570
If there's not land over here soon, I'm actually gonna break down in tears.

912
00:53:49,790 --> 00:53:53,870
Maybe the plan then is to go kill some creepers so we can fly and actually find it.

913
00:53:53,950 --> 00:53:54,090
Wait!

914
00:53:54,230 --> 00:53:54,350
Oh!

915
00:53:55,630 --> 00:53:56,550
We may have something.

916
00:53:59,630 --> 00:54:00,530
That could be it.

917
00:54:03,950 --> 00:54:05,210
It's looking good, I think.

918
00:54:10,020 --> 00:54:12,740
But will it be visible from the water?

919
00:54:20,760 --> 00:54:21,800
Lots of birch.

920
00:54:25,900 --> 00:54:27,180
Oh, thank god we got land.

921
00:54:27,300 --> 00:54:27,620
Okay, okay.

922
00:54:28,080 --> 00:54:29,200
I think I know where we are then.

923
00:54:30,600 --> 00:54:31,540
It's fully landed.

924
00:54:34,320 --> 00:54:35,760
Oh, I do remember mountains.

925
00:54:42,120 --> 00:54:43,960
Mountains... I think I remember this.

926
00:54:45,940 --> 00:54:46,980
The pink trees.

927
00:54:49,140 --> 00:54:50,380
There's also a village there.

928
00:54:57,020 --> 00:54:58,300
I think it's over there somewhere.

929
00:55:11,000 --> 00:55:11,800
Wait, what?

930
00:55:16,240 --> 00:55:17,360
The hell is that?

931
00:55:20,620 --> 00:55:23,480
That does not look like a village to me.

932
00:55:29,060 --> 00:55:30,320
What actually is that?

933
00:55:35,640 --> 00:55:36,440
Oh, it is!

934
00:55:36,600 --> 00:55:37,100
Okay, never mind.

935
00:55:38,640 --> 00:55:43,480
For a second, I was like... It looked like my first house I made in Create.

936
00:55:44,620 --> 00:55:45,020
Remember?

937
00:55:45,940 --> 00:55:48,360
But it couldn't have been, because that was in a different world.

938
00:55:49,640 --> 00:55:51,660
So I was so flabbergasted for a second.

939
00:55:57,120 --> 00:55:58,560
We're not gonna check out this place.

940
00:55:58,840 --> 00:55:59,360
Actually, we are.

941
00:56:02,120 --> 00:56:03,120
Do they have carrots?

942
00:56:09,440 --> 00:56:10,080
Shit.

943
00:56:10,640 --> 00:56:12,180
It's all wheat.

944
00:56:12,800 --> 00:56:14,440
Yeah, these are wheat people, look.

945
00:56:14,920 --> 00:56:15,960
They got wheat here.

946
00:56:19,300 --> 00:56:20,340
Uh, what do you sell?

947
00:56:21,860 --> 00:56:23,700
You want carrots as well?

948
00:56:24,940 --> 00:56:25,580
Dude.

949
00:56:29,430 --> 00:56:30,690
I gotta go to bed, I guess.

950
00:56:31,750 --> 00:56:33,590
I will sleep in your bed.

951
00:56:33,590 --> 00:56:35,650
I will eat your oatmeal.

952
00:56:39,010 --> 00:56:46,190
Could be back there.

953
00:56:46,650 --> 00:56:47,650
I need to get up high.

954
00:56:51,130 --> 00:56:52,590
That was a bad idea.

955
00:56:53,250 --> 00:56:55,830
Thought I could get enough speed to gain some height there at the end.

956
00:57:07,630 --> 00:57:09,710
Maybe I should make a house near these trees at some point.

957
00:57:09,870 --> 00:57:10,570
It is kind of nice.

958
00:57:13,170 --> 00:57:14,770
It's also a little girly, isn't it?

959
00:57:14,990 --> 00:57:15,910
To make a house here.

960
00:57:18,740 --> 00:57:21,220
Not that that's a problem, just stating that.

961
00:57:23,720 --> 00:57:24,560
It's nice.

962
00:57:25,320 --> 00:57:26,260
Not gonna lie.

963
00:57:29,000 --> 00:57:31,580
Sometimes you gotta bring out your inner girl, you know?

964
00:57:33,060 --> 00:57:35,040
Listen, I'm a fan of Mean Girls.

965
00:57:35,300 --> 00:57:38,100
It's like one of my... What do you call it?

966
00:57:40,400 --> 00:57:43,460
Enjoyable things that I'm sort of ashamed of, but not really.

967
00:57:43,800 --> 00:57:44,380
Type deals.

968
00:57:45,900 --> 00:57:46,700
Love that movie.

969
00:57:46,970 --> 00:57:47,270
Oops.

970
00:57:55,850 --> 00:57:57,850
Dude, where... is this hotel?

971
00:57:58,570 --> 00:57:59,490
Did I really fly?

972
00:57:59,570 --> 00:58:01,210
I guess I flew for a while, didn't I?

973
00:58:01,590 --> 00:58:02,830
It was kind of a long trip.

974
00:58:04,190 --> 00:58:06,190
Thinking back on it, it was a long trip.

975
00:58:08,310 --> 00:58:09,230
A portal!

976
00:58:11,270 --> 00:58:12,410
In these woods?

977
00:58:15,220 --> 00:58:17,100
Oh, man, imagine we had carrots in this.

978
00:58:18,560 --> 00:58:20,640
I'll take... No, I don't want that, actually.

979
00:58:21,840 --> 00:58:22,640
Is it a little touch shovel?

980
00:58:22,960 --> 00:58:23,740
That's interesting.

981
00:58:25,040 --> 00:58:26,680
Wait, why does the portal look like this?

982
00:58:27,220 --> 00:58:29,100
Look at that, it's going like this and then up.

983
00:58:30,520 --> 00:58:31,560
I've never seen this.

984
00:58:33,480 --> 00:58:34,480
Very weird design.

985
00:58:38,260 --> 00:58:39,000
That's a first.

986
00:58:45,680 --> 00:58:50,380
I mean, if I can't find this hotel, I'm gonna refund all the potatoes, obviously.

987
00:58:52,700 --> 00:58:54,240
But come on, we gotta find it.

988
00:58:56,800 --> 00:58:57,680
Can't be that hard.

989
00:58:58,860 --> 00:58:59,600
Maybe over here?

990
00:59:04,300 --> 00:59:04,980
Let me see.

991
00:59:07,720 --> 00:59:10,300
And the funny thing is, I found it in no time as well.

992
00:59:11,180 --> 00:59:12,420
I found it so fast.

993
00:59:18,650 --> 00:59:19,710
I don't think it's over here.

994
00:59:19,850 --> 00:59:21,530
It must be that way, if anything.

995
00:59:24,910 --> 00:59:25,350
Yeah.

996
00:59:27,050 --> 00:59:28,650
Good news is we can fly from up here.

997
00:59:29,710 --> 00:59:32,450
In fact, let's just... Ooh, guys.

998
00:59:34,350 --> 00:59:35,910
Nah, then we're gonna have an ugly pillar.

999
00:59:36,110 --> 00:59:36,730
I don't like that.

1000
00:59:39,090 --> 00:59:41,170
Big old pillar in the middle of nowhere.

1001
00:59:41,790 --> 00:59:42,710
It's not my jam.

1002
00:59:44,830 --> 00:59:48,610
When I make towers, I do them in places where it looks nice.

1003
01:00:18,060 --> 01:00:18,920
Okay, here we go.

1004
01:00:19,520 --> 01:00:20,400
Do we see anything?

1005
01:00:28,320 --> 01:00:30,180
It's gotta be like in this direction, right?

1006
01:00:30,660 --> 01:00:30,980
Go!

1007
01:00:36,840 --> 01:00:38,120
Now we've got speed.

1008
01:00:39,720 --> 01:00:40,880
Really look around.

1009
01:00:43,000 --> 01:00:43,780
And up.

1010
01:00:50,230 --> 01:00:51,690
Not seeing anything.

1011
01:00:55,870 --> 01:00:57,110
And up.

1012
01:01:03,290 --> 01:01:04,610
I'm gonna go this way.

1013
01:01:11,060 --> 01:01:12,320
Let's get on that mountain up there.

1014
01:01:12,980 --> 01:01:16,140
Dude, the amount of distance I just got from that one flight is crazy.

1015
01:01:18,700 --> 01:01:22,400
You know, it's actually worth it to bring the... the flying cloak.

1016
01:01:23,180 --> 01:01:25,180
Even when you don't have fireworks.

1017
01:01:25,900 --> 01:01:29,440
Simply because of how much distance you can gain from just going up a little bit.

1018
01:01:31,740 --> 01:01:32,400
Go up here.

1019
01:01:46,370 --> 01:01:47,630
We are going to check this direction.

1020
01:01:47,770 --> 01:01:51,250
If nothing appears at all in that direction, we are going to go more like that.

1021
01:01:54,030 --> 01:01:54,730
That's an E.

1022
01:01:57,210 --> 01:01:57,610
Huh.

1023
01:01:59,650 --> 01:02:00,430
What does that mean?

1024
01:02:06,610 --> 01:02:08,410
And come on, show me.

1025
01:02:18,700 --> 01:02:19,860
I am lost, guys.

1026
01:02:20,000 --> 01:02:21,280
I'm actually completely lost.

1027
01:02:28,040 --> 01:02:29,280
I'm gonna try this direction.

1028
01:02:39,200 --> 01:02:39,680
Yep.

1029
01:02:40,500 --> 01:02:41,180
Good landing.

1030
01:02:41,800 --> 01:02:42,840
Ooh, everything's on fire there.

1031
01:02:42,980 --> 01:02:43,560
What the hell?

1032
01:02:45,020 --> 01:02:46,360
Lava's coming out of that rock!

1033
01:03:05,960 --> 01:03:07,140
I feel like I'm close.

1034
01:03:10,280 --> 01:03:12,440
Tall trees could be an indicator, I guess.

1035
01:03:14,600 --> 01:03:15,240
Okay, go.

1036
01:03:20,910 --> 01:03:24,650
I do remember actually having lots of mushrooms around the same area.

1037
01:03:26,110 --> 01:03:27,070
Or just in general.

1038
01:03:27,230 --> 01:03:30,910
I feel like I associate mushrooms in my mind with hotels.

1039
01:03:33,050 --> 01:03:34,710
I don't know why, I just do.

1040
01:03:47,620 --> 01:03:50,380
Should I break the law here and actually go straight up and fly?

1041
01:03:51,580 --> 01:03:52,700
It's criminal, isn't it?

1042
01:03:54,580 --> 01:03:55,400
I can't do it.

1043
01:03:55,460 --> 01:03:56,520
I can't do it in good conscience.

1044
01:03:56,680 --> 01:03:57,440
I just can't do it.

1045
01:04:06,660 --> 01:04:08,380
But now we've gone in this direction a little bit.

1046
01:04:08,700 --> 01:04:10,440
Getting up would be nice, just temporarily.

1047
01:04:12,540 --> 01:04:13,280
Let me have a look.

1048
01:04:37,290 --> 01:04:38,870
I really don't want to go back.

1049
01:04:39,710 --> 01:04:43,910
I think the smart thing is to go back to the islands and reorient myself.

1050
01:04:45,510 --> 01:04:46,790
I'm too deep, man.

1051
01:04:46,870 --> 01:04:47,390
I can't do it.

1052
01:04:47,450 --> 01:04:47,970
I can't do it.

1053
01:04:48,290 --> 01:04:48,930
Actually, wait.

1054
01:04:49,070 --> 01:04:49,350
I can.

1055
01:04:50,130 --> 01:04:50,930
I have an idea.

1056
01:04:52,250 --> 01:04:54,530
We know which way this one's supposed to...

1057
01:05:00,260 --> 01:05:03,620
I feel like when I went home, it was kind of this direction, I guess.

1058
01:05:04,140 --> 01:05:05,180
Maybe I am on the right path.

1059
01:05:08,580 --> 01:05:09,700
This does feel right.

1060
01:05:10,240 --> 01:05:11,000
I'm not gonna lie.

1061
01:05:11,440 --> 01:05:12,640
Maybe it's just... Trust.

1062
01:05:13,080 --> 01:05:14,060
Trust in the process.

1063
01:05:16,880 --> 01:05:17,820
Trust the mushrooms.

1064
01:05:26,840 --> 01:05:27,500
Don't hit me.

1065
01:05:28,160 --> 01:05:28,720
Thank you.

1066
01:05:35,120 --> 01:05:36,360
Show me what's good.

1067
01:05:38,120 --> 01:05:39,400
We got mushrooms now.

1068
01:05:48,160 --> 01:05:48,900
That's weird.

1069
01:05:53,920 --> 01:05:55,680
Okay, we got water back there again.

1070
01:05:55,780 --> 01:05:57,140
I feel like we're in the wrong spot.

1071
01:05:57,300 --> 01:05:57,440
Oh!

1072
01:05:57,740 --> 01:05:58,040
Whoops.

1073
01:06:03,110 --> 01:06:03,910
Okay, here's the plan.

1074
01:06:03,990 --> 01:06:05,530
I'm gonna go a little bit more in that direction.

1075
01:06:05,690 --> 01:06:09,090
If I don't see anything, we're gonna turn around that way and look there.

1076
01:06:13,390 --> 01:06:14,310
And hey, you know what?

1077
01:06:14,350 --> 01:06:15,530
We're looking for carrots anyway.

1078
01:06:16,250 --> 01:06:19,890
So if we see a village and stuff, we're just gonna... We're just looking for carrots, right?

1079
